{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Abram dwelt in the land of Canaan.</b> In the rest of the land of Canaan as a whole — that he did not remain in one place, but sojourned throughout all the land of Canaan. And Lot settled in one place of it, in the cities of the plain, for the cities of the plain are included within the land of Canaan. And the sense of <b>in the cities of the plain</b> is: now in this one and now in that one, because of the weight of the flocks. And this is the sense of ״ויבחר לו לוט את כל ככר הירדן״ — for he stipulated with Abram that he would not come into the whole plain:" "<b>And he pitched his tent toward Sodom.</b> Scripture teaches you the disgrace of Lot, for he chose the company of the wicked and pitched his tent among them; therefore it immediately follows, ״ואנשי סדום״. And Scripture teaches you the merit of Abram, that his lot did not fall in a place of wickedness but only in the Holy Land:"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:13.346552544Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}